# Copy this file to .env before running the app.
#
# Point this at wherever the backend (uvicorn) is reachable from your phone/simulator:
#   - iOS Simulator on the same Mac as the backend -> http://localhost:8000
#   - Physical phone via Expo Go -> http://<your-Mac's-LAN-IP>:8000
#     (Find your LAN IP with: ipconfig getifaddr en0)
#   - Both your Mac and phone must be on the same Wi-Fi network.
EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Optional — for the production build only, not local dev. The shop
# server's own LAN address (e.g. http://192.168.31.31:8000). If set, the
# app falls back to it automatically whenever EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL is
# unreachable (see src/api/client.ts) — meaningful because the backend
# runs on the shop's own on-site server, so the shop's WiFi can stay up
# even when its internet doesn't. Leave unset to skip the fallback.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LOCAL_BACKEND_URL=
